2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535516 true] [17592186353222 1113 #uuid "8bc5c35e-337a-5a6f-8888-1b0686935cc0" 13194139535516 true] [17592186353222 1145 "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3\\cdot (2{x}_{3})=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=6{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\cdot 6+5\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 1}{{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{82}{41}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535516 true] [17592186353223 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353224 13194139535516 true] [17592186353223 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353225 13194139535516 true] [17592186353223 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353226 13194139535516 true] [17592186353223 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353227 13194139535516 true] [17592186353223 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353228 13194139535516 true] [17592